    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 62.18 score makes him our most potent asset against Brandon Woo. Despite a challenging matchup, the projection software heavily weights **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s favorable platoon split and his elite spot in the two-hole, which optimizes his counting stat floor. Following him, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (59.38) and **Jacob Wilson** (59.54) represent high-floor plays, with **Jacob Wilson** receiving a significant boost from park factors that elevate his overall output despite the lack of a defined opposing pitcher projection. **Miguel Vargas** earns a strong 57.90 start; while he faces a somewhat difficult arm in Ryan Weathers, the combination of favorable wind conditions and a \"slow delivery\" factor against the pitcher significantly enhances his stolen base potential\u2014a critical consideration given our strategic emphasis on speed.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s slate involved **Josh Jung**, who landed on the bench with a 42.87 score. While **Josh Jung** remains a viable depth piece, the depth of our middle infield and the relative efficiency of **Brayan Rocchio** (41.40) and **Nolan Schanuel** (56.87) squeezed him out; **Brayan Rocchio** was given the nod specifically for his positional flexibility and order placement, though his score remains marginal due to a tough draw against Joe Drohan. We are maintaining a cautious stance on **Nolan Schanuel** and the lower-ranked **Wade Meckler** (37.47) as we await official lineup confirmation, as their projected utility is highly sensitive to batting order fluctuations. With **Kyle Tucker** and **Jackson Merrill** out of the equation due to scheduling, we are relying on our depth to maintain momentum in the SB category while avoiding the trap of chasing starts that fall below our 40-point efficiency floor.",
